    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with tests green. Here's how I addressed each finding.\n\n## Finding 1 \u2014 stale variable name \u2705 Fixed\nRenamed `declaredHouseholdMember` \u2192 `joiningExistingHousehold` in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (declaration and the read at the soft-match guard). The name now reflects what drives it: any owner that has existing household members, with no user declaration involved.\n\n## Finding 2 \u2014 stale declaration comment \u2705 Fixed\nRewrote the comment above the flag so it describes the current rule (\"joining an existing household\u2026 a legitimate household join, not a suspected duplicate\") instead of the removed `sharesHousehold` gating, and updated the matching phrasing in the soft-match comment.\n\n## Finding 3 \u2014 orphaned `sharesHousehold` / `HouseholdDuplicateException` \u2705 Pruned\nI agreed this residue became dead specifically because of my change, so I removed it rather than just tracking it:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `sharesHousehold` request-schema field (it was write-only, silently ignored by the new flow).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 removed the transient `sharesHousehold` field and its `isSharesHousehold()`/`setSharesHousehold()` accessors (no remaining reader).\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 removed the `handleHouseholdDuplicateException` handler and its import (nothing throws it anymore).\n- Deleted **`HouseholdDuplicateException.java`**.\n\nA `grep` confirms no dangling references to `sharesHousehold`, `HouseholdDuplicate`, or the old variable name remain. Since `sharesHousehold` was removed from both the generated DTO (via openapi) and the `Owner` entity together, MapStruct has nothing to half-map, and the build/tests confirm it compiles cleanly.\n\nThe capping mechanism itself \u2014 which the review approved \u2014 is unchanged, and the acceptance test still passes (second household member created, level capped at first + 1).",
