    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe capping mechanism itself is placed well \u2014 deriving-and-capping inside `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` is cohesive, the persisted `membershipLevelCap` field mirrors the existing `householdMemberCount` pattern, and the getter/setter + schema additions are consistent across all four dialects. The problem is the leftover state in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`:\n\n1. **Stale variable name \u2014 `declaredHouseholdMember` (ClinicServiceImpl.java:269, 286).** The semantics have inverted. It no longer means \"the request *declared* (via `sharesHousehold`) that it shares the household\" \u2014 the new code sets it `true` for *every* owner that has existing household members, with no declaration involved. A maintainer reading `declaredHouseholdMember` will expect a user-supplied flag to be behind it. Rename to something like `isHouseholdMember` / `joiningExistingHousehold` so the name matches what now drives it.\n\n2. **Stale declaration comment (ClinicServiceImpl.java:266-268).** The comment still describes the removed behavior: \"accepted into an existing household because the request declared it shares one (`sharesHousehold`). A declared member is deliberately not treated as a suspected duplicate.\" `sharesHousehold` is no longer consulted on this path at all. Update the comment to describe the derived-membership rule now in effect.\n\n3. **Orphaned `sharesHousehold` concept (secondary).** Removing the rejection block removed the only reader of `owner.isSharesHousehold()`; the field/getter/setter on `Owner` (lines 116, 488-493) and the `HouseholdDuplicateException` doc referencing it are now dead relative to this flow. Not strictly part of the capping feature, but leaving a flag that no longer influences anything, plus a `HouseholdDuplicateException` that this path can no longer throw, is the kind of residue that misleads the next maintainer. At minimum note/track it; ideally prune it as part of this change so the household path stays coherent.\n\nFindings 1 and 2 are directly in the touched lines and should be fixed here.",
